],"gloss":"sweet"},{"surface":"துணை","parts":[{"text":"துணை","lemma":"துணை","gloss":"companion"}],"gloss":"companion"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்ற","parts":[{"text":"மன்ற","lemma":"மன்ற","gloss":"surely"}],"gloss":"surely"},{"surface":"மரையா","parts":[{"text":"மரையா","lemma":"மரையா","gloss":"wild cow"}],"gloss":"wild cow"},{"surface":"இரிய","parts":[{"text":"இரி","lemma":"இரி","gloss":"flee"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to flee"},{"surface":"ஏறு","parts":[{"text":"ஏறு","lemma":"ஏறு","gloss":"bull"}],"gloss":"bull"},{"surface":"அட்டு","parts":[{"text":"அட்டு","lemma":"அட்டு","gloss":"having killed"}],"gloss":"having killed","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செங்கண்","parts":[{"text":"செம்","lemma":"செம்மை","gloss":"red"},{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"eye"}],"gloss":"red-eyed"},{"surface":"இரும்புலி","parts":[{"text":"இரும்","lemma":"இருமை","gloss":"dark"},{"text":"புலி","lemma":"புலி","gloss":"tiger"}],"gloss":"dark tiger"},{"surface":"குழுமும்","parts":[{"text":"குழுமு","lemma":"குழுமு","gloss":"roar"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"habitual suffix"}],"gloss":"roars"},{"surface":"அதனால்","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"that"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"inflectional increment"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"ஆல்","gloss":"causal suffix"}],"gloss":"therefore"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மறைத்தல்","parts":[{"text":"மறை","lemma":"மறை","gloss":"hide"},{"text":"த்தல்","lemma":"த்தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"hiding"},{"surface":"காலையோ","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"காலை","gloss":"time"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"interrogative suffix"}],"gloss":"is it the time?"},{"surface":"அன்றே","parts":[{"text":"அன்று","lemma":"அன்று","gloss":"it is not"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"it is not indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"திறப்பல்","parts":[{"text":"திற","lemma":"திற","gloss":"open"},{"text":"ப்ப்","lemma":"ப்ப்","gloss":"future tense marker"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"first person singular suffix"}],"gloss":"I will open"},{"surface":"வாழி","parts":[{"text":"வாழ்","lemma":"வாழ்","gloss":"live"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"subjunctive suffix"}],"gloss":"may you live"},{"surface":"வேண்டு","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டு","lemma":"வேண்டு","gloss":"request"}],"gloss":"please"},{"surface":"அன்னை","parts":[{"text":"அன்னை","lemma":"அன்னை","gloss":"mother"}],"gloss":"mother"},{"surface":"நம்","parts":[{"text":"நம்","lemma":"நாம்","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"},{"surface":"கதவே","parts":[{"text":"கதவு","lemma":"கதவு","gloss":"door"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"door indeed"}]}],"literal":"He of the chest with sandalwood from the red mountain / He with the garland of bees buzzing on the blue water lilies of the pool / coming at midnight, returns from our house / O innocent young woman! Your sweet companion who rests on your chest / having killed the bull so that the wild cows of the common ground flee / the red-eyed dark tiger roars. Therefore, / is this the time for concealing? It is not! / I will open, may you live, please, mother, our door!","translation":"He whose chest is smeared with red sandalwood from the mountains, who wears a garland of blue water lilies from the pool, buzzing with bees, comes at midnight and returns from our house. O innocent girl, he is the sweet companion who rests on your breast! In the common ground, a red-eyed dark tiger has killed a wild bull, making the wild cows flee, and now it roars. Therefore, this is no longer the time to hide your love. May you prosper, mother! I shall open our door to let him in.","modern":"மலையின் சிவந்த சந்தனம் பூசிய மார்பை உடையவனும், சுனையில் மலர்ந்த குவளை மலர்களில் வண்டுகள் மொய்க்கும் மாலையை அணிந்தவனுமாகிய தலைவன், நடுநிசியில் வந்து நம் இல்லத்திலிருந்து திரும்பிச் செல்கிறான். பேதைமை குணம் கொண்ட பெண்ணே! அவன் உன் மார்பில் அமரும் இனிய துணைவன் ஆவான். மன்றத்தில் காட்டுப் பசுக்கள் அஞ்சி ஓடும்படி ஆண் காட்டெருதை அடித்துக் கொன்று, சிவந்த கண்களை உடைய கரிய புலி முழங்குகின்றது. அதனால், இனி நாம் இக்காதலை மறைத்து வைக்கும் காலம் அல்ல. தாயே! நீ வாழ்க! நான் நம் கதவைத் திறக்கின்றேன்.","explanation":"The friend speaks to the heroine and her mother in a situation where the hero has been visiting secretly at night. The friend points out the immense danger of his nightly journey through the mountain paths, where a fierce, red-eyed tiger has just killed a wild bull and is roaring nearby. By addressing the mother directly and offering to open the door, the friend subtly reveals the secret love affair to ensure the family accepts the hero and hastens their marriage. The imagery of the tiger killing the bull in the common ground reflects the dangerous mountain landscape of the Kuriñci tiṇai and underscores the urgency of stopping these perilous secret visits. Key words like 'நடுநாள்' (midnight), 'இரும்புலி' (dark tiger), and 'மறைத்தற் காலையோ அன்றே' (this is not the time to hide) highlight the transition from secret courtship to public acknowledgment.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}